// A bandit shakedown - the example mod gives one of the base game's characters a conversation,
// without touching the base game's files. Talk to any Bandit and this is what they open with.
//
// The headers under each title are the conversation's metadata: kind (Greeting, Topic or Ambient),
// attach (who it belongs to, in the same condition language barks use), requires, priority and
// once. A node without them - Choices, below - is an ordinary Yarn node a conversation jumps into.
//
// gold() is a question the game answers; every fact is a function, with '.' written as '_'.
// <<TakeMoney>>, <<SetFlag>> and <<ChangeStanding>> are effects the game carries out (Raiders is
// the Bandit's faction id). $asked_about_road is Yarn's own memory, which lasts one conversation;
// anything the squad should remember for longer is a flag. A choice tagged #reason: shows greyed
// out, with that reason, when its condition fails; one without is left off. Each #line: tag is the
// line's id - what crosses the network, what a translation keys on, what a recording is filed under.
//
// Compile with: ysc compile shakedown.yarn -o . -n shakedown

title: Shakedown
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Definition == Bandit
---
<<declare $asked_about_road = false>>
Bandit: Toll road. Twenty gold, or you walk back the way you came. #line:shakedown_toll
<<jump Choices>>
===

title: Choices
---
-> Pay the toll. <<if gold() >= 20>> #line:shakedown_pay #reason:not_enough_money
    <<TakeMoney 20>>
    <<SetFlag example_paid_toll>>
    Bandit: Pleasure doing business. Road's yours. #line:shakedown_paid
-> Who says it's your road? <<if not $asked_about_road>> #line:shakedown_ask
    <<set $asked_about_road to true>>
    Bandit: The twelve of us in those rocks say so. #line:shakedown_twelve
    <<jump Choices>>
-> Get out of my way. #line:shakedown_refuse
    <<ChangeStanding Raiders -10>>
    Bandit: Wrong answer. #line:shakedown_wrong
===

// Once a squad has paid, every Bandit knows it: the higher priority wins over the shakedown.
title: ShakedownPaid
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Definition == Bandit
requires: Flag(example_paid_toll)
priority: 10
---
Bandit: You paid. Keep walking before I forget that. #line:shakedown_already_paid
===
